docs {
  Story S14, TICK-419 (kit TICK-437, docs/acceptance/S14/README.md). The story's four acceptance steps with the story users: `admin@tenant-a.test`, `auditor@tenant-a.test` (tenant A's auditors group), `agent@tenant-a` is Alice (`alice@tenant-a.test`), `agent@tenant-b` is Bob (`bob@tenant-b.test`). AC1 (CI-A11, S14.17-S14.23): the admin publishes an incident version, Alice creates and updates an incident, the auditor sees all three on one timeline in order, with actor, source and diff. AC2 (S14.24): entity-type versions written before the backfill ran are in the log as backfilled entries. AC3 (S14.25-S14.29): Alice gets 403 on the timeline and reads the incident's history; Bob gets 403 and the same 404 as for an id that exists nowhere. AC4 (S14.30-S14.31): a secret value in a published schema is refused with `config_secret_in_content`, naming the path only. Needs `tools/seed.sh`, and for AC2 versions the backfill has seen: either a stack upgraded from a pre-S14 commit (docs/acceptance/S14/tools/upgrade-setup.sh) or `audit_backfill_s8()` re-run as nava_migrator after the seed (the stack case `s14_acceptance`). Runs again on the same stack. CI-A2 is not asserted for configuration tables (D-5-8: their commit check arrives in S15).
}
